## OSHA Training

**Q: Do I need OSHA training?**
A: Yes, legally. Anyone operating a forklift needs OSHA certification. OSHA requires classroom AND hands-on training. Online-only certifications are not fully compliant.

**Q: How much does training cost?**
A: $799 for up to 5 students. $79 per additional student. Individual training: $150/person.

**Q: How long does training take?**
A: 4-8 hours depending on group size and experience level.

**Q: How long is certification valid?**
A: 3 years OSHA. Annual refresher recommended even if not required yet.

**Q: Can you train in Spanish?**
A: Yes, bilingual instructors available for on-site sessions. Let us know in advance.

**Q: What if someone fails training?**
A: We provide extra coaching at no additional charge. Most people pass with the extra help.

