## Wire-Guided Systems

**Q: What is wire guidance?**
A: A wire embedded in the floor that guides forklift movement in narrow aisles. Allows very precise positioning and higher stacking.

**Q: How much does it cost?**
A: $4.25 per linear foot installed. A typical warehouse aisle (200 feet) would be $850. Full installation with design: varies by complexity.

**Q: How long does installation take?**
A: Design is 1-2 weeks. Installation is typically 2-3 weeks for a standard warehouse.

**Q: Does it work in cold storage?**
A: Yes, cold-storage rated systems available for freezer applications.

**Q: Can it work with any forklift?**
A: Most Raymond units come wire-guidance ready. Other brands need retrofit kits. We can advise on your specific equipment.

